<title>GERMANY: D. Babcock narrows Oct-Jan loss by 100 mln DMK.</title>
<headline>D. Babcock narrows Oct-Jan loss by 100 mln DMK.</headline>
<dateline>OBERHAUSEN, Germany 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Troubled German enginering group Deutsche Babcock AG said on Wedensday it narrowed a loss in the October-to-January period by a good 100 million marks, after losing 250 million marks in the same period in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Chief executive Klaus G. Lederer announced the improvement at the annual shareholders meeting. In the previous business year, which ended September 30, Babcock lost 434 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
